<speak>The small jobs are better for me. If I decide to redo the whole balcony, I get carried away measuring things and making lists. Then it becomes another project. If I just go outside to tidy a corner, I notice the plants properly. One of the herbs has been doing very well, and we use a little in the kitchen. That's satisfying in a simple way. Nobody needs a meeting about it, and nobody is waiting for a report.</speak>